  "caption": "Quinn bought 40 seedlings and planted them all in one day. Monday was slow.\n\nGarden aches in the back, thumbs, wrists, shoulders and knees are usually about load rather than damage: a season's worth of jobs squeezed into one weekend. Making the load smaller tends to matter more than keeping a perfectly straight back.\n\nWhat often helps: rotating tasks and pacing the day, ratchet secateurs, padded handles and two-handed loppers, a thick kneeling pad (switching between kneeling, a stool and standing), keeping gently active with a sore back, and saving big overhead jobs until your shoulders are ready.\n\nGet checked for leg pain with numbness or weakness, bladder or bowel changes, fever, night pain, or a shoulder ache lasting around six weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
